---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'About Restaurant Tip Calculator';
const description =
  'What Restaurant Tip Calculator does, how its calculator works in your browser, and how its tipping guidance is researched.';

const nav = [
  { href: '/', label: 'Calculator' },
  { href: '/methodology/', label: 'Methodology' },
];

const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  '@id': 'https://restauranttipcalculator.com/about/#breadcrumb',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Restaurant Tip Calculator', item: 'https://restauranttipcalculator.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: 'https://restauranttipcalculator.com/about/' },
  ],
});
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/about/" jsonLd={jsonLd} nav={nav}>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="guide-intro"><a href="/">Restaurant tip calculator</a> / About</p>
    <h1>About Restaurant Tip Calculator</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Restaurant Tip Calculator is a focused tool for working out a tip, payable total, and exact bill split without
      turning a simple restaurant check into a spreadsheet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="purpose">
    <h2>What this site is for</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The calculator supports percentage tips and custom dollar tips, optional tax and fee inputs, delivery-fee
        handling, exact cent-reconciled splitting, and optional whole-dollar round-up. The goal is to make the math
        explicit rather than hide assumptions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Calculator inputs are processed locally in your browser. The site does not require an account and does not
        send bill amounts to a custom calculation server.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="research">
    <h2>How the guidance is handled</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Tipping advice can mix together etiquette, survey responses, transaction data, wage rules, and restaurant
        policy. This site keeps those categories separate and links to the underlying sources where factual claims
        depend on them.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> documents the calculator's rounding and splitting rules,
        research source hierarchy, review approach, and the distinction between observed behavior and recommendations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site does not claim a restaurant-industry credential, expert review, or a universal tipping rule where the
        evidence does not support one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
